!LOOP1!\tab\tab    In certain OS/8 files, sequences of up to nine <NUL> characters\par
                     followed by a <LF> character are placed after every <FF>\par
                     character, all of which must be removed.  The program\par
                     iteratively loops back to the portion of the program labeled\par
                     \i !LOOP1!\i0  until all <NUL> characters after the <FF> character are\par
                     removed.\par
\par
0A&127"NOLFTEST$'\tab    If the next character after a <FF> character is not a <NUL>\par
\tab\tab\tab    character, transfer control to the portion of the program\par
\tab\tab\tab    labeled \i !LFTEST!\i0 .\par
\par
                     Note: All tests of this form must mask the high-order bit using\par
                     the constant 127 (octal 177) because all characters not yet\par
                     tested might have the mark parity bit set.\par
\par
DOLOOP1$\tab\tab    If the next character currently after a <FF> character is a\par
                     <NUL> character, delete the character; transfer control back to\par
                     the portion of the program labeled \i !LOOP1!\i0  to test for\par
                     additional <NUL> characters.\page\b Line #14:\tab\tab    !LFTEST!0A&127-10"NONOTFF$'C$\b0\par
\par
!LFTEST!\tab\tab    After all <NUL> characters after a <FF> character are removed,\par
                     the next character is likely a <LF> character; test for this\par
                     now.\par
\par
0A&127-10"NONOTFF$\par
\par
\tab\tab\tab    If the character after all <NUL> characters after a <FF\par
                     character is not a <LF> (ASCII code 10 decimal, 12 octal),\line                      transfer control to the portion of the program labeled \i !NOTFF!\i0 .\par
\par
                     Note: This applies if the file differs from the explicitly\par
                     checked character sequence found in certain files created\par
                     within OS/8.\par
\par
'C$\tab\tab\tab    If the character after all <NUL> characters after a <FF\par
                     character is a <LF> character, advance the buffer pointer (C)\par
                     to preserve the <LF> character.\par
\par
\b Line #15:\tab\tab    !LOOP2!0A&127"NOENDTEST$'DOLOOP2$\b0\par
\par
!LOOP2!\tab\tab    In certain files passed through the OS/8 PTP: handler, a long\par
                     sequence of trailing <NUL> characters may follow the last <FF>\par
                     character followed by nine <NUL> characters followed by <LF>.\par
                     All of these additional <NUL> characters will also be removed.\par
\par
0A&127"NOENDTEST$\tab    If the character after the <LF> character is not a <NUL>\par
                     character, transfer control to the portion of the program\par
                     labeled \i !ENDTEST!\i0 .\par
