\b Line #16:\tab\tab    !ENDTEST!0A+1"NONOTEOF$'QS"EONOCH$'0,QSP0,QSK\b0\par
\par
!ENDTEST!\tab\tab    An extremely pragmatic sequence known to be contained within\par
                     certain OS/8 files processed by the PTP: handler must be\par
                     located at the end of the file.  If this is not the case, all\par
                     further character processing will be handled conventionally.\par
\par
0A+1"NONOTEOF$\tab    If the code returned for the next character following (0A) the\par
                     latest <NUL> character is -1, the end of file has been reached.\par
                     If this is not the case, transfer control to the portion of the\par
                     program labeled \i !NOTEOF!\i0 .\par
\par
'QS"EONOCH$'         Q-register S contains the buffer pointer value where the\par
                     trailing <FF> character was located before the now-validated\par
\tab\tab\tab    trailing sequence of additional characters.  If the contents of\par
                     Q-register S is zero, control is transferred to the portion of\par
                     the program labeled \i !NOCH!\i0  (because the edit buffer does not\par
                     contain any characters to be processed into the output file).\par
\par
0,QSP0,QSK\tab\tab    All characters from the beginning of the buffer through the\par
\tab\tab\tab    position indicated in Q-register S will be output using the\par
\tab\tab\tab    Punch (P) command.  All characters from the beginning of the\par
\tab\tab\tab    buffer through the position indicated in Q-register S will then\par
                     be deleted using the Kill (K) command.  Program flow continues\par
                     at the label \i !NOCH!\i0  which follows.\par
\par
\b Line #17:\tab\tab    !NOCH!EFEX$!NOTEOF!QSJOPUTIN$\b0\par
\par
!NOCH!EFEX$\tab\tab    All retained characters in the edit buffer (if any) have been\par
                     processed.  Close the file with an End File (EF) command.  TECO\par
                     EXits (EX) to the operating system.  All characters (within the\par
                     pragmatic sequence specially checked for) were removed.\page !NOTEOF!QSJOPUTIN$   If the pragmatic sequence of characters expected after the <FF>\par
                     did not occur, control is transferred here.  The edit buffer\par
                     pointer is restored (J) to the position saved earlier in\par
                     Q-register S.  Control is then transferred to the portion of\par
                     the program labeled \i !PUTIN!\i0  to handle the latest <FF> character\par
                     routinely.\par
\par
\b Line #18:\tab\tab    !NOTFF!Q1-10"NOPUTIN$'-1A-13"EOPUTIN$'13I$\b0\par
\par
!NOTFF!\tab\tab    Control is transferred to this portion of the program if either\par
                     the latest character is not a <FF> character or the pragmatic\par
                     sequence possibly present after a <FF> character in certain\par
                     OS/8 files was not detected.\par
\par
Q1-10"NOPUTIN$\tab    If the latest character is not a <LF> character, control is\par
\tab\tab\tab    transferred to the portion of the program labeled \i !PUTIN!\i0 .\par
\par
'-1A-13"EOPUTIN$\tab    If the latest character is a <LF> character, check if the\par
\tab\tab\tab    previous character (-1A) is a <CR> character (ASCII code 13\par
\tab\tab\tab    decimal, 15 octal).  If this is the case, transfer control to\par
                     the portion of the program labeled \i !PUTIN!\i0 .\par
\par
                     Note: It is not necessary to mask this value against the\par
