                     removed the high-order bit of all previous characters; all\par
                     newly inserted characters do not have the high-order bit set.\par
\par
'13I$\tab\tab\tab    If the latest character is a <LF> character and the previous\par
\tab\tab\tab    character is not a <CR> character, insert a <CR> character\par
                     before the <LF> character.  Certain PDP-8-sourced files\par
                     fail to obey the <CR> followed by <LF> convention; this is \par
\tab\tab\tab    especially likely before or after a <FF> character; the host\par
\tab\tab\tab    operating system requires lines to strictly end with <CR>\par
